 | M14b Options + game menu | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+5 tests in `options.rs`, 1 in `touch_ui.rs`) | `options.rs`: b1.7.3's `GameSettings` (`options.txt`), `GuiOptions`, `GuiVideoSettings`, `GuiControls`, `GuiSlider` and `GuiIngameMenu`, from the pause button and the title screen's "Options...". Replaces the old pause menu (its Reset world button is gone); Pregen, Fly and LoD debug stay top-left; new `LoD: ON/OFF` button in Options. Sensitivity, invert, render distance, GUI scale, performance cap and difficulty act; music, sound, bobbing, anaglyph, advanced OpenGL, graphics, smooth lighting and the keys are stored only. See ROADMAP changelog. |
 | Options list (Sodium layout, 2026-11-01) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+9 tests in `options.rs`, +4 in `ui.rs`; `tools/optlist_proto.py` runs here: layout, text widths, tips and the clip maths against the real font); **NOT b1.7.3** | `options.rs` + new `ui.rs` + `menu.rs`: the options screen is Sodium's `VideoSettingsScreen` in b1.7.3's skin. ONE scrolling list of every setting (General, Graphics, Performance, Effects, Controls, Controller buttons, Controller tuning), each row its name on the left and a stone button or slider on the right; a page list down the left jumps to a section and lights the section in view as the list scrolls (LB / RB step it); group headings; a description pane (beside the list on a wide screen, a strip under it on a narrow one) explains the last tapped setting; settings that are saved but read by nothing (Graphics, Smooth Lighting, Advanced OpenGL, 3D Anaglyph, the keys) are dim, like Sodium's unavailable options. A drag scrolls (a drag that starts on a slider and goes along it moves the slider, one that goes up scrolls), a tap acts on lift. The Keys / Controller tabs and the Tuning... page are gone (one list), Dig Delay lives under Controls only. Without a scissor in the HUD pass, `ui::clip` cuts the quads at the list's edges. The same look (title with rules and studs, bevelled panels, coloured world-kind tags, empty-list hint, shared scroll bar) on the title screen, world list, create / rename / delete screens and the game menu. Not done: search, kinetic scrolling, a mouse wheel (no events for it), restyling the atmosphere editor. Controls (look and keys, pad buttons, pad tuning) is a tab of its own beside Settings; Graphics has an FOV slider (30 .. 110, 70 by default) and Brightness and Gamma percent sliders (50% .. 150%, final pass of both renderers). |
 | M15 Controller (Controllify port) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+7 tests in `gamepad.rs`, 1 in `options.rs`) | `input/gamepad.rs`: isXander's Controllify, the parts b1.7.3 has. Sticks walk and look (Controllify's deadzone, 6 look curves, 10 deg/tick at 100%), triggers dig / hit / place, bumpers and the hotbar wheel pick slots, a virtual mouse drives every menu and container, touch buttons hide while a pad is in use, rumble on damage / block break / explosion (`rumble.rs`, JNI). New **Controls > Controller** tab (buttons page + tuning page), saved as `pad_*` in `options.txt`. Button hints (2026-11-02): a bottom-right list of what the bound buttons do while a pad is in use (`Pad::hints`), drawn with the Controller Tooltip Selector pack's Xbox, PlayStation or Switch pictures (`assets/padbtn.rgba`, `tools/gen_pad_buttons.py`, the HUD texture's `PAD_Y` block) or as text; **Button Hints** and **Button Icons** in Controls > Controller tuning, saved as `pad_hints`, `pad_iconStyle`. New **Drop** bind (D-Down by default, `pad_drop`): throws one item of the selected slot. **Hint placement and size (2026-11-02):** the hints no longer sit on a fixed corner: each screen hands in the rects it draws (`menu::Menu::avoid`, `options::OptionsUi::avoid` / `Pause::avoid`, `stats_ui::StatsUi::avoid`, the hotbar while playing) and the hints slide along the bottom (then the top edge) to the first spot 4 GUI units clear of all of them, shrink to half their size, turn into the other layout, or are left out; **Hint Size** (50% .. 200% of the GUI scale, `pad_hintSize`) and **Hint Layout** (Auto = a row in menus and a list while playing, Horizontal, Vertical; `pad_hintLayout`) in Controls > Controller tuning. Written without a toolchain, not compiled. Not ported: gyro, DualSense extras, on-screen keyboard, chat / drop / perspective (not in mc-rs / b1.7.3); sprint is the row below, on L3. |
-| World Preview (2026-11-04) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+2 tests in `preview.rs`) | `preview.rs`: port of World Preview Prime's idea (background tiles, biome / height maps, biome list highlight, read-out) as a screen opened by **World Preview** at Create World's top left. Reads the seed (a blank field's random seed is fixed when Create World opens), the world type and every `NaturalSettings` field (workers build `OverworldGenerator::preview` + its chunk manager after `natural::set`); the type can be cycled and **Settings** opens World-Gen Settings and returns with the map rebuilt. Height comes from the density column (`height_at`), not a made chunk. Views: Biomes, Relief, Height, Temperature, Humidity. Touch: drag pans, pinch zooms (`TouchUi::take_pinch`, second finger = `PointerRole::Pinch`), double tap zooms, tap reads out a point, scrolling legend. Not in it: rivers, structures, caves, seed editing, fling. |
+| World Preview (2026-11-04) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+2 tests in `preview.rs`) | `preview.rs`: port of World Preview Prime's idea (background tiles, biome / height maps, biome list highlight, read-out) as a screen opened by **World Preview** at Create World's top left. Reads the seed (a blank field's random seed is fixed when Create World opens), the world type and every `NaturalSettings` field (workers build `OverworldGenerator::preview` + its chunk manager after `natural::set`); the type can be cycled and **Settings** opens World-Gen Settings and returns with the map rebuilt. Height comes from the density column (`height_at`), not a made chunk. Views: Biomes, Relief, Height, Temperature, Humidity. Touch: drag pans, pinch zooms (`TouchUi::take_pinch`, second finger = `PointerRole::Pinch`), double tap zooms, tap reads out a point, scrolling legend. Second pass (same day, also uncompiled): rivers and lakes from `Hydro` (`Region::water_at`), Blooming structure starts (`structory::starts`, legend filter, no real names: `structory.bin` keeps none), seed typed or re-rolled in the preview, fling and eased zoom, contour lines, chunk grid, live read-out, and the same map from the game menu's Tools page (**World Preview**) with the player and the explored area (`Explored`, `<world>/explored`, fog toggle). Not in it: caves, structure pieces. |
 | Item + recipe viewer (REI, 2026-11-04) | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device (+3 tests in `rei.rs`; favorites, tags, categories, `@mod` and auto-crafting added 2026-11-04, +9 tests: `rei.rs` +7, `craft.rs` +1, `items.rs` +1); **NOT b1.7.3** | `rei.rs`: after Roughly Enough Items 26.2 (entry list, `DefaultDisplayViewingScreen`, crafting / fuel categories), drawn with the Immersive Interfaces REI support pack (bundled in `tools/packs/immersive_rei`, `tools/gen_rei.py` -> `assets/rei.rgba`, a 256 x 64 block of the HUD texture before the map block, `SHEET_H` 3276). Opened by **Tools > Inventory Cheat...** (gives items) or the small **R** button of the inventory and crafting table screens (views; the table's is new, for auto-crafting 3x3 recipes). Paged entry list (arrows or a horizontal swipe), soft-keyboard search, tap = recipes, long press = uses, **Mode: View / Give / Fav** (give: tap 1, long press a stack; fav: tap stars the item); the recipe view has category tabs (a registry, `Category` / `register_category`: Crafting, Smelting, Fuel, Block Drops from `items::block_drops`, Tag), page row, workstation, `+1` / `Stack` in give mode, and a star for the item and one on every display; Back walks the history. **Search**: words match the name, `@mod` the namespace (`@minecraft`, `@cortes` = ids 400..=430), `#tag` the tags (`TAGS`: ores, fuel, wool, dyes, ingots, slabs, food, armor, tools, swords, pickaxes, axes, shovels, hoes, `cortes:weapons`; b1.7.3 has none, these are this port's), a leading `-` excludes. **Favorites** (items and whole recipes): the **Favs** tab of the list (tap opens, long press removes), kept per world in `reiFavorites` of the world folder (`i`, `c`, `s`, `f`, `x` lines, 64 at most, bad lines dropped on load). **Auto-crafting**: only while the viewer is open over a crafting grid (inventory 2x2 or table 3x3) a crafting display has a `+` (long press: as many sets as the stock allows) that lays the recipe out from the main inventory through `craft::Screen::auto_fill` (all or nothing, the grid goes back to the inventory first), then closes the viewer; ingredients you lack are red and `+` says why it refuses. The star sprites are drawn by `tools/gen_rei.py` (the pack has none). **REI Theme** (Light / Dark, `reiTheme`) in Options > Effects. Not ported: favorites of REI's own entry types (Game Mode, Weather, Time), mob-loot category (loot is rolled per mob, `mobs.rs`), tag recipes in `#tag` autocompletion, auto-crafting from chests. |
 | ImmediatelyFast ideas | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+7 tests, 1 extended) | `render/hud.rs`: the HUD text is one textured quad per glyph from a font atlas at the end of the HUD texture (was a quad per run of lit pixels: about 7x fewer text vertices); `render/items.rs`: `SignCache` keeps a sign's text quads between frames (5 s expiry); `gpuErrorTrace:true` in `options.txt` logs a backtrace with each wgpu error (`gpu/context.rs`). The rest of ImmediatelyFast (batching, map and animated-item atlases, framebuffer switching, Apple GL upload, resource pack handling) has no counterpart in mc-rs. Idea source: ImmediatelyFast 26.3, RaphiMC, LGPL-3.0. See the performance changelog. |
 | FerriteCore ideas | written without a toolchain: not compiled, not run (+2 tests) | Lazy `Nibbles` (no array while all metadata is 0), flat `lod::Cols` for a real chunk's columns (no `Vec` per column; `Tile0::put` no longer clones 4096), exact-size LoD vectors. The rest of FerriteCore (blockstate / model / component dedupe, thread detector) has no counterpart in mc-rs. Idea source: FerriteCore, malte0811, MIT. See ROADMAP changelog. |
